# Security Review Skill

Reference with **@claude-skills/security-review** when doing security-focused review or hardening.

## When to use

- User asks for security review, vulnerability check, or hardening
- Reviewing auth, secrets, input validation, or sensitive data handling
- Checking for common issues (injection, XSS, insecure config, exposed secrets)

## Principles

- Check authn/authz, input validation, and output encoding
- Ensure secrets and tokens are not hardcoded or logged; use env/config
- Prefer parameterized queries and safe APIs (e.g. ORM, validated inputs)
- Align with project tools (e.g. Bandit for Python); call out severity and fix priority
- For full test-architecture security workflow use @bmad testarch workflows when appropriate
